IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-dates`
IMPORT `voca-mai-s37`
IMPORT `voca-core`
IMPORT `voca-seat`

-- Cases for the applicant's seat (voca-seat.l4), with the regulative rules of voca-core.l4 and voca-mai-s37.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (act-2009-035.txt; for MAI s 37, act-1994-009.txt),
-- never copied from the encoding's output; the arithmetic is in the comment above each assertion. No scenario life
-- raised this Act: every person here is the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL throughout.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the
-- trace ends FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days.
--
-- Readings used in the date arithmetic (see voca-dates.l4): "within 3 years after" a day ends on its anniversary;
-- "within 28 days after" ends 28 days later; "before the person turns 21" ends the day before the 21st birthday.

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 1. A primary victim. HYPOTHETICAL: Mia, born 12 June 1990, is punched and kicked outside a Brisbane bar on
-- 15 March 2025 (assault occasioning bodily harm). She has a fractured cheekbone and develops post-traumatic stress
-- disorder. She reports it to police that night and helps the investigation. Her expenses: counselling $3,000,
-- medical $4,500, travel $300, reports $800; lost earnings $12,000 in the 2 years; a $250 jacket ruined; $2,000 to
-- move house (no exceptional circumstances found); legal costs $700.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 25: an offence against the person, in Queensland, directly causing injury. s 26(1): injured as a direct result of
-- the act being committed against her: a primary victim, and in no other capacity.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` (LIST `primary victim`))
-- Schedule 2 s 3(3)(e): assault occasioning bodily harm is category C. Category A circumstances: no very serious injury
-- or disease. Category B circumstances: a serious injury (bodily injury and mental illness, 2 kinds of s 27(1)), but
-- she was 34, not under 16 or over 60, and not impaired, so (b) fails. Category C circumstances are only for a
-- category D act. So category C, $6,000 (s 2).
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category C` `category C` 6000)
-- s 39: 3,000 + 4,500 + 300 + 800 = 8,600; (e) loss of earnings 12,000 (under $20,000); (f) clothing 250; (g) the
-- $2,000 relocation only with exceptional circumstances: 0; (h) special assistance 6,000. 8,600 + 12,000 + 250 + 6,000
-- = 26,850, under $120,000 (s 38(1)). s 38(2): legal costs up to $500 of the $700. 26,850 + 500 = 27,350.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE FALSE 3000 4500 300 800 12000 250 2000 0 0 0 700 FALSE 0 0 `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 27350)
-- With exceptional circumstances (s 28), the $2,000 relocation counts under s 39(g): 27,350 + 2,000 = 29,350.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE TRUE 3000 4500 300 800 12000 250 2000 0 0 0 700 FALSE 0 0 `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 29350)
-- Loss of earnings is capped at $20,000 (s 39(e)): with $35,000 lost, 8,600 + 20,000 + 250 + 6,000 + 500 = 35,350.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE FALSE 3000 4500 300 800 35000 250 2000 0 0 0 700 FALSE 0 0 `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 35350)
-- The $120,000 limit (s 38(1)): medical expenses of $150,000 on top: components 8,600 + 150,000 + 12,000 + 250 + 6,000
-- = 176,850, limited to 120,000; plus legal costs 500 = 120,500. The legal costs sit outside the limit (s 38(2)).
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE FALSE 3000 154500 300 800 12000 250 2000 0 0 0 700 FALSE 0 0 `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 120500)
-- s 54(1)(a): within 3 years after 15 March 2025, so to 15 March 2028. Applying 1 October 2025: in time. Applying 16
-- March 2028: out of time (unless extended under s 54(2)). A s 54(2) extension to 30 June 2028 makes 16 March in time.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2028))
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2028) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2028))
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 16 3 2028) EQUALS (`out of time: the last day was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2028))
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2028) (DATE_FROM_DMY 16 3 2028) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2028))
-- The s 54 rule. Day 0 is 15 March 2025; 15 March 2028 is day 365 + 365 + 366 (29 February 2028) = 1096.
#ASSERT `the number of days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2028) EQUALS 1096
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 54 -- the victim must apply for victim assistance within the time limit` 1096) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for victim assistance` 200)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 54 -- the victim must apply for victim assistance within the time limit` 1096) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for victim assistance` 1096)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 54(1) ...: the application for victim assistance was not made in time ..." (day 1097)
#TRACE `s 54 -- the victim must apply for victim assistance within the time limit` 1096 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply for victim assistance` AT 1097
-- ss 78-82: eligible, reported to police, helped the investigation: nothing stops a grant.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`
-- ss 85, 86, 100. Medicare paid $2,000 of her medical expenses (a relevant payment, Schedule 3 (b)(vi)), all of it
-- for an expense she can claim. No reduction for conduct. Interim assistance of $1,500 was paid. 27,350 - 2,000 =
-- 25,350; less 1,500 interim = 23,850.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid after reductions` 27350 0 2000 0 1500 EQUALS 23850
-- With a 25% reduction for her own conduct (s 85) and $500 of the $2,000 accepted as made for another purpose
-- (s 86(2A)): s 85 first, 27,350 x 0.75 = 20,512.50; then s 86, 20,512.50 - 1,500 = 19,012.50; no interim.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid after reductions` 27350 25 2000 500 0 EQUALS 19012.5
-- READING (finding 9): the relevant payment comes off the amount after the $120,000 limit. 120,500 - 20,000 = 100,500.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid after reductions` 120500 0 20000 0 0 EQUALS 100500
-- No reduction can go below nothing: payments of $40,000 against 27,350 leave 0.
#ASSERT `How much will I be paid after reductions` 27350 0 40000 0 0 EQUALS 0
-- ss 97, 98: she applied, asked for interim assistance, has urgent and immediate expenses of $7,200, and the
-- assessor is satisfied they cannot wait: up to $6,000. With $1,500 of urgent expenses: $1,500.
#ASSERT `Can I get interim assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 7200 EQUALS (`interim assistance can be granted, up to` 6000)
#ASSERT `Can I get interim assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1500 EQUALS (`interim assistance can be granted, up to` 1500)
-- s 97(d): not asked for in the application, Part 14 does not apply; (b): decided, it does not apply; s 98(1): the
-- assessor not satisfied, none.
#ASSERT `Can I get interim assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 1500 EQUALS `no interim assistance: Part 14 does not apply (s 97)`
#ASSERT `Can I get interim assistance` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 1500 EQUALS `no interim assistance: Part 14 does not apply (s 97)`
#ASSERT `Can I get interim assistance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 1500 EQUALS `no interim assistance: the government assessor is not satisfied the expenses must be incurred before the decision (s 98(1))`
-- s 124: notice of the decision on 10 January 2026; 28 days after is 7 February 2026. Applying 7 February: in time.
-- Applying 8 February: out of time. With the time extended (s 124(3)) to 28 February: in time.
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for an internal review` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 2 2026) EQUALS (`in time: I can apply for internal review up to and including` (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 2 2026))
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for an internal review` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 8 2 2026) EQUALS (`out of time: the 28 days ended on` (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 2 2026))
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for an internal review` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 8 2 2026) EQUALS (`in time: I can apply for internal review up to and including` (DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026))
-- A decision not in Schedule 1 (for example choosing the government assessor under s 62) is not reviewable.
#ASSERT `By when must I ask for an internal review` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2026) EQUALS `not reviewable: the decision is not one identified in Schedule 1`
-- The s 124 rule. Day 0 is the day of notice. She applies on day 20; the review must be decided by day 20 + 42 = 62.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 124 -- an internal review applied for in time must be decided within 42 days` 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for internal review` 20), (EVENT `the scheme manager` `decide the review` 62)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not applying is no breach: the 28 days pass (the next event, at day 40, ends them) and nothing is owed.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 124 -- an internal review applied for in time must be decided within 42 days` 28) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the scheme manager` `decide the review` 40)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the scheme manager, "s 124(8): an application for internal review must be decided within 42 days ..." (decided on day 63)
#TRACE `s 124 -- an internal review applied for in time must be decided within 42 days` 28 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply for internal review` AT 20
    PARTY `the scheme manager` DOES `decide the review` AT 63
-- ss 89(2), 141B: assistance granted 1 February 2026. A $5,000 income protection insurance payment on 10 March 2027
-- is within 6 years: notice within 28 days, by 7 April 2027 (10 March + 21 = 31 March, + 7 = 7 April).
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the scheme manager about a payment` `after assistance is granted` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 3 2027) EQUALS (`I must tell the scheme manager, in writing or orally, by` (DATE_FROM_DMY 7 4 2027))
-- The 6 years end on 1 February 2032 (READING: the anniversary). A payment that day: notice by 29 February 2032 (a
-- leap year). A payment on 2 February 2032: no duty under s 89(2).
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the scheme manager about a payment` `after assistance is granted` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2032) EQUALS (`I must tell the scheme manager, in writing or orally, by` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2032))
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the scheme manager about a payment` `after assistance is granted` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 2 2032) EQUALS `no duty under ss 89(2), 98(2) or 141A: the payment came more than 6 years after the grant`
-- s 141A: a payment before any decision or interim assistance, 20 November 2025: notice by 18 December 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I tell the scheme manager about a payment` `before my application is decided and before any interim assistance is granted` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2025) EQUALS (`I must tell the scheme manager, in writing or orally, by` (DATE_FROM_DMY 18 12 2025))
-- The notification rule. Day 0 is the day of the payment.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `ss 89(2), 98(2), 141A -- the applicant must tell the scheme manager of a relevant payment within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `give the scheme manager notice of the relevant payment` 28)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 141A(2) or the condition under s 89(2) or 98(2) ..." (notice on day 29)
#TRACE `ss 89(2), 98(2), 141A -- the applicant must tell the scheme manager of a relevant payment within 28 days` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `give the scheme manager notice of the relevant payment` AT 29
-- s 101: granted to an adult on 1 February 2026, so an amendment application within 6 years, by 1 February 2032.
-- Applying 1 June 2027 with none made that year: she may. With one already made that calendar year: no (s 101(5)),
-- unless the scheme manager allows another (s 101(6)) or she was given an amendment notice (s 101(7)).
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027) 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`I may apply to amend my grant, up to and including` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2032))
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027) 1 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I have already applied this calendar year (s 101(5))`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027) 1 TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`I may apply to amend my grant, up to and including` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2032))
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027) 1 FALSE TRUE EQUALS (`I may apply to amend my grant, up to and including` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2032))
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 2 2032) 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`no: out of time; the last day was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2032))
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 6 2027) 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: my circumstances have not changed and are not likely to (s 101(1)(b))`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 2. A child primary victim of a series of sexual offences. HYPOTHETICAL: Ava, born 3 April 2012, is sexually
-- abused (not rape) by her sports coach from 1 October 2024 to 31 March 2025. She tells her school counsellor, who
-- is her counsellor, but nobody tells police. She is diagnosed with an anxiety disorder.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Schedule 2 s 3(2)(b): a sexual offence other than rape is category B. Category A circumstances: none. So $9,000.
-- (Category B circumstances apply only to a category C or D act.)
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `a sexual offence other than rape` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2012) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category B` `category B` 9000)
-- If her anxiety disorder has permanently and significantly reduced her quality of life and treatment would not change
-- that, it is a very serious injury: category A circumstances, $15,000 (Schedule 2 s 1(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `a sexual offence other than rape` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2012) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category B` `category A` 15000)
-- But not if treatment would make it no longer very serious (very serious injury, para 2): back to $9,000.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `a sexual offence other than rape` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2012) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category B` `category B` 9000)
-- s 54(1)(c): a child when it happened, so within 3 years after turning 18 (3 April 2030): to 3 April 2033. That is
-- later than (a), 1 October 2027. Applying 1 January 2033: in time.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2012) FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2033) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2033))
-- s 81: reported only to her counsellor. She is a special primary victim (s 81(2)(a)(i) a sexual offence; (ii) a person
-- in a position of trust; (b)(i) a child), so a report to her counsellor counts. Nothing stops a grant.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`
-- Contrast an adult assaulted by a stranger who told only a doctor, with no reasonable excuse: not a special primary
-- victim, so it is not reported (s 81(1)(a)(i)): no grant. With a reasonable excuse (s 81(1)(b)): nothing stops it.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no grant: the act was not reported, and there is no reasonable excuse (ss 21(3)(a), 81)`
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`
-- s 51(2): a child, 13 at application and represented by a lawyer: her parent, she herself, or someone approved.
#ASSERT `Who may make my application` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the child's parent, on the child's behalf`, `the child, being at least 12 and represented by a lawyer`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`)
#ASSERT `Who may make my application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the child's parent, on the child's behalf`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`)
-- s 101(3)(b): granted on 1 February 2026 to her as a child, so an amendment application before she turns 24 (3 April
-- 2036): to 2 April 2036. Applying 3 April 2036: out of time.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2012) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 4 2036) 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`I may apply to amend my grant, up to and including` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 4 2036))
#ASSERT `Can I apply to amend my grant` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2012) (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 4 2036) 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS (`no: out of time; the last day was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 4 2036))

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 3. A related victim who also pays for the funeral. HYPOTHETICAL: Liam, born 5 May 1995, is the adult son of
-- a man stabbed on 20 November 2024 in Townsville, who died of his wounds on 22 November 2024. They were close. Liam
-- was not dependent on him. Liam pays $18,000 for the funeral. His other costs: counselling $4,000, medical $1,000,
-- a report $600; he asks $20,000 for distress; legal costs $400.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 26(5), (7): a family member (child) with a genuine personal relationship with a primary victim who died as a
-- direct result: a related victim.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` (LIST `related victim`))
-- Had Liam also seen the stabbing and been injured by it, he would be a witness secondary victim too, but eligible in
-- only one capacity (s 23).
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` (LIST `witness secondary victim`, `related victim`))
-- s 50: he incurs funeral expenses for a primary victim who died as a direct result: up to $15,000 of the $18,000.
-- If his sister had already been granted $6,000 for the same funeral, the combined total limit (s 50(4)) leaves $9,000.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) TRUE FALSE 18000 0 EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 15000)
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) TRUE FALSE 18000 6000 EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 9000)
-- s 50(2): the person who committed the act gets none.
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) TRUE TRUE 18000 0 EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 0)
-- s 48(1): up to $75,000 less the $15,000 funeral expense assistance granted to him: limit $60,000. s 49: 4,000 +
-- 1,000 + 0 + 600 = 5,600; (e) nothing (not dependent); (f) distress capped at $15,000; (g) none. 5,600 + 15,000 =
-- 20,600, under 60,000. s 48(2): legal costs 400. 20,600 + 400 = 21,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `related victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) FALSE FALSE 4000 1000 0 600 0 0 0 0 20000 15000 400 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 21000)
-- The funeral reduction bites only at the limit: with $70,000 of claimed components (counselling 50,000 + medical
-- 1,000 + report 600 + distress 15,000 + exceptional other expenses 3,400 = 70,000), the limit of 60,000 holds:
-- 60,000 + 400 = 60,400.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `related victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) FALSE TRUE 50000 1000 0 600 0 0 3400 0 20000 15000 400 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 60400)
-- s 54(1)(b): within 3 years after the death (22 November 2024): to 22 November 2027, later than 3 years after the act
-- (20 November 2027). Applying 21 November 2027: in time.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `related victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 1995) FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 21 11 2027) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2027))
-- s 58(1)(a): funeral expense assistance within 3 years after the death: to 22 November 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for funeral expense assistance` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2024) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2024) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2027))
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for funeral expense assistance` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2024) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 23 11 2027) EQUALS (`out of time: the last day was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2027))
-- The s 58 rule. Day 0 is 22 November 2024; 22 November 2027 is day 365 x 3 = 1095 (no 29 February in between).
#ASSERT `the number of days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2024) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 22 11 2027) EQUALS 1095
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 58 -- funeral expense assistance must be applied for within 3 years of the death` 1095) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for funeral expense assistance` 1095)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 58(1): the application for funeral expense assistance was not made within 3 years ..." (day 1096)
#TRACE `s 58 -- funeral expense assistance must be applied for within 3 years of the death` 1095 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `apply for funeral expense assistance` AT 1096
-- s 80(2): if the father's involvement in drug dealing was the main reason he was stabbed, and Liam knew of it, no grant
-- to Liam. s 80(3): not if Liam knew only because he witnessed the stabbing.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no grant: the primary victim's criminal activity was the only or main reason for the act, and I was or should have been aware of it (ss 21(2)(c), 80(2))`
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 4. Witness secondary victims. HYPOTHETICAL: Noah sees a man assaulted at a bus stop on 1 February 2025 (a
-- less serious act) and develops an anxiety disorder. Zoe sees her flatmate murdered on 1 March 2025 (a more
-- serious act), and also paid $15,000 for the funeral, granted as funeral expense assistance.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 26(4): injured as a direct result of witnessing the act: a witness secondary victim.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` (LIST `witness secondary victim`))
-- Noah, s 44(1)(b) and s 46: counselling 2,500 + medical 500 + travel 100 + report 400 = 3,500, under $20,000. His
-- $5,000 lost earnings and $300 legal costs are not in s 46 or s 44(2): nothing for them. 3,500.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `witness secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2025) FALSE FALSE 2500 500 100 400 5000 0 0 0 0 0 300 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 3500)
-- Even with exceptional circumstances, s 46 has no loss of earnings or other expenses component: still 3,500.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `witness secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2025) FALSE TRUE 2500 500 100 400 5000 0 2000 0 0 0 300 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 3500)
-- Zoe, s 44(1)(a): up to $75,000 less $15,000 funeral expense assistance: limit $60,000. s 45 with exceptional
-- circumstances: counselling 10,000 + medical 5,000 + travel 1,000 + report 1,000 = 17,000; (e) loss of earnings
-- $25,000 capped at 20,000; (f) other expenses 8,000. 17,000 + 20,000 + 8,000 = 45,000, under 60,000. s 44(2): legal
-- costs of $900 capped at 500. 45,500.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `witness secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) TRUE TRUE 10000 5000 1000 1000 25000 0 8000 0 0 15000 900 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 45500)
-- Without exceptional circumstances, (e) and (f) fall away: 17,000 + 500 = 17,500.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `witness secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) TRUE FALSE 10000 5000 1000 1000 25000 0 8000 0 0 15000 900 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 17500)
-- s 32(3): had Zoe seen the murder at work and been paid workers' compensation, she gets only s 45(f) (8,000, with
-- exceptional circumstances) and legal costs (500): 8,500. s 32(4): Noah, a witness to a less serious act paid
-- workers' compensation, gets funeral expense assistance only: 0 here.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `witness secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) TRUE TRUE 10000 5000 1000 1000 25000 0 8000 0 0 15000 900 TRUE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 8500)
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `witness secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 2 2025) FALSE FALSE 2500 500 100 400 5000 0 0 0 0 0 300 TRUE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 0)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 5. A primary victim injured at work. HYPOTHETICAL: Ethan, born 1 January 1985, a security guard, is beaten
-- at work on 10 January 2025 and suffers grievous bodily harm. He is entitled to workers' compensation, applies, and
-- accepts a $4,000 lump sum offer; his application is finally dealt with on 30 June 2026. His costs: counselling
-- $2,000, medical $6,000, report $500, loss of earnings $30,000, clothing $300, relocation $3,000 (exceptional
-- circumstances accepted), legal costs $600.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Schedule 2 s 3(2)(c): grievous bodily harm is category B, $9,000; no very serious injury.
-- s 32(2), (6)(b): paid workers' compensation, he gets s 39(f) clothing 300 and (g) relocation 3,000, and special
-- assistance less the lump sum: 9,000 - 4,000 = 5,000. 300 + 3,000 + 5,000 = 8,300; legal costs 500 (s 38(2)). 8,800.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE TRUE 2000 6000 0 500 30000 300 3000 0 0 0 600 TRUE 4000 0 `grievous bodily harm` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 8800)
-- Finding 3: a lump sum of $12,000, more than the special assistance, leaves none: 300 + 3,000 + 500 = 3,800.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE TRUE 2000 6000 0 500 30000 300 3000 0 0 0 600 TRUE 12000 0 `grievous bodily harm` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 3800)
-- A lump sum exactly equal to the special assistance ($9,000) also leaves none (s 32(6)(b) needs less than): 3,800.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE TRUE 2000 6000 0 500 30000 300 3000 0 0 0 600 TRUE 9000 0 `grievous bodily harm` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 3800)
-- Not paid workers' compensation (s 32 does not apply): 2,000 + 6,000 + 500 = 8,500; loss of earnings capped at
-- 20,000; clothing 300; relocation 3,000; special assistance 9,000. 40,800 + 500 = 41,300.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE TRUE 2000 6000 0 500 30000 300 3000 0 0 0 600 FALSE 0 0 `grievous bodily harm` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 41300)
-- s 34(1): with the workers' compensation application finally dealt with, he may apply; s 34(2)(a): within 3 years
-- after 30 June 2026, to 30 June 2029 (despite s 54(1), which would end on 10 January 2028).
#ASSERT `May I apply yet, if I am entitled to workers' compensation` `primary victim` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `I may apply: my workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with (s 34(1))`
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) TRUE TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2028) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2029))
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) TRUE TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2029) EQUALS (`out of time: the last day was` (DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2029))
-- Before the workers' compensation application is finally dealt with, or before making one, he may not apply yet.
#ASSERT `May I apply yet, if I am entitled to workers' compensation` `primary victim` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: I must wait until my workers' compensation application is finally dealt with (ss 33, 34(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `May I apply yet, if I am entitled to workers' compensation` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not yet: I must first make a workers' compensation application (s 34(1)(a)), or, if its time has passed, ask the scheme manager for approval (s 34(4))`
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) TRUE TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS `not yet: a workers' compensation application must first be made and finally dealt with (s 34(1)), unless the scheme manager approves under s 34(4)`
-- With the scheme manager's s 34(4) approval he may apply; READING (finding 6): s 54(1) then applies, to 10 January 2028.
#ASSERT `May I apply yet, if I am entitled to workers' compensation` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `I may apply: the scheme manager has approved my applying without a workers' compensation application (s 34(4))`
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) TRUE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2028))
-- s 31: Part 3 does not apply to a parent secondary victim.
#ASSERT `May I apply yet, if I am entitled to workers' compensation` `parent secondary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3 does not apply: no workers' compensation condition on applying`
-- s 34(2)(b): an apprentice born 1 August 2008, assaulted at work on 1 October 2024, whose workers' compensation
-- application is finally dealt with on 1 July 2025 (aged 16): 3 years after is 1 July 2028; before turning 21 is to 31
-- July 2029. The later: 31 July 2029.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2008) TRUE TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2029) EQUALS (`in time: the last day to apply is` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 7 2029))
-- s 32(5), (7): a related victim paid $24,000 workers' compensation for the death, asking $25,000 for what the person
-- who died would have given (capped at 20,000) and $10,000 for distress: non-expense assistance 30,000 less 24,000 =
-- 6,000. Plus counselling 1,000 and report 500: 7,500; legal costs 500: 8,000. With $30,000 paid: 0, so 2,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `related victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE FALSE 1000 0 0 500 0 0 0 25000 10000 0 500 TRUE 0 24000 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 8000)
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `related victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 1 2025) FALSE FALSE 1000 0 0 500 0 0 0 25000 10000 0 500 TRUE 0 30000 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 2000)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 6. A motor vehicle used as a weapon. HYPOTHETICAL: Grace is deliberately run down on 5 May 2025 and badly
-- injured. The car is identified and insured (CTP). Her symptoms are immediate. She first sees a lawyer on 1 July 2025.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- MAI s 37(2)(b): the earlier of 9 months after the accident (5 February 2026) and 1 month after first consulting a
-- lawyer (1 August 2025): 1 August 2025. Asked on 20 July 2025 with no notice given: due by 1 August 2025.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 7 2025) EQUALS (`notice of the claim is due by` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2025))
-- Notice given on 1 August 2025: in time. Notice given on 15 September 2025: late, and s 37(3) keeps the obligation,
-- with a reasonable excuse for the delay; for an identified vehicle there is no bar.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) EQUALS `notice was given within the s 37(2) period`
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 9 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) EQUALS (`notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (MAI s 37(3))` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2025))
-- Without a lawyer: 9 months after the accident, 5 February 2026. If symptoms first appeared on 20 June 2025: 9 months
-- after that, 20 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) EQUALS (`notice of the claim is due by` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 2 2026))
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 6 2025) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) EQUALS (`notice of the claim is due by` (DATE_FROM_DMY 20 3 2026))
-- An unidentified car (a claim against the Nominal Defendant): s 37(2)(a), 3 months, to 5 August 2025; s 37(3), barred
-- if no notice within 9 months, after 5 February 2026. On 1 December 2025 with no notice: late. On 1 March 2026 with
-- no notice: barred. Notice on 1 January 2026, asked 1 March 2026: late but not barred.
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 12 2025) EQUALS (`notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (MAI s 37(3))` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 8 2025))
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS (`the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months after the accident (MAI s 37(3))` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 2 2026))
#ASSERT `By when must I give notice of my motor accident claim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2026) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) EQUALS (`notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (MAI s 37(3))` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 8 2025))
-- Part 3A. No claim made and not barred: the decision is deferred until she claims and the claim is finally dealt
-- with (s 36D(2)); counselling is decided now (s 36F).
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no motor accident claim has been made` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `deferred until I make a motor accident claim and it is finally dealt with (s 36D(2)); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `made, and not yet finally dealt with` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 8 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `deferred until my motor accident claim is finally dealt with (s 36E); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
-- s 36C: the insurer denied liability, or a settlement offer was accepted: finally dealt with, no deferral.
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `the insurer has denied liability for it` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no deferral: the motor accident claim has been finally dealt with (s 36C)`
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `an offer or counter offer of settlement has been accepted` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no deferral: the motor accident claim has been finally dealt with (s 36C)`
-- s 36D(3): the unidentified-car claim is barred on 1 March 2026; if the scheme manager accepts her excuse, no
-- deferral; if not, the deferral stands.
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no motor accident claim has been made` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no deferral: the claim is barred or late notice failed, and the scheme manager accepts my excuse (s 36D(3))`
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no motor accident claim has been made` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `deferred until I make a motor accident claim and it is finally dealt with (s 36D(2)); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
-- s 36D(3)(a)(ii): an identified car is never barred by s 37(3), but a late notice tried without success, with the
-- excuse accepted, also ends the deferral. An excuse alone, with nothing in (a), does not.
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no motor accident claim has been made` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no deferral: the claim is barred or late notice failed, and the scheme manager accepts my excuse (s 36D(3))`
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no motor accident claim has been made` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `deferred until I make a motor accident claim and it is finally dealt with (s 36D(2)); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
-- s 36A: no CTP-covered liability (not a motor vehicle accident in the MAI s 4 sense): Part 3A does not apply.
#ASSERT `Will the decision wait for my motor accident claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE `no motor accident claim has been made` (DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025) TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2025) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Part 3A does not apply: no deferral for a motor accident claim`
-- Part 3B. She applied for victim assistance on 1 September 2025 and has an undecided NIISQ application: the decision
-- may wait, but after 1 September 2027 must be made as soon as reasonably practicable (s 36I(3)); all but medical
-- expenses is decided anyway (s 36J(2)). Where the motor accident deferral also applies, s 36J does not (s 36J(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `Can the decision wait for my NIISQ application` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) EQUALS (`the decision may wait for the NIISQ application, but after this day must be made as soon as reasonably practicable (s 36I); all but medical expenses is decided anyway (s 36J)` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027))
#ASSERT `Can the decision wait for my NIISQ application` `primary victim` TRUE FALSE TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) EQUALS (`the decision may wait for the NIISQ application, but after this day must be made as soon as reasonably practicable (s 36I); only counselling is decided anyway, because the motor accident deferral applies (s 36F)` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2027))
#ASSERT `Can the decision wait for my NIISQ application` `primary victim` TRUE TRUE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) EQUALS `no deferral under s 36I: the NIISQ application has been decided`
#ASSERT `Can the decision wait for my NIISQ application` `related victim` TRUE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2025) EQUALS `Part 3B does not apply: no deferral for an NIISQ application`
-- The MAI s 37 rule, identified car: day 0 is 5 May 2025; 1 August 2025 is day 26 + 30 + 31 + 1 = 88.
`Grace's notice facts` MEANS `Motor accident notice facts` WITH
    `the day of the accident`                                    IS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025
    `the motor vehicle can be identified`                        IS TRUE
    `symptoms of the injury were immediately apparent`           IS TRUE
    `the day symptoms of the injury first appeared`              IS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025
    `the claimant has consulted a lawyer about a possible claim` IS TRUE
    `the day the claimant first consulted a lawyer about it`     IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2025
`the unidentified car's notice facts` MEANS `Motor accident notice facts` WITH
    `the day of the accident`                                    IS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025
    `the motor vehicle can be identified`                        IS FALSE
    `symptoms of the injury were immediately apparent`           IS TRUE
    `the day symptoms of the injury first appeared`              IS DATE_FROM_DMY 5 5 2025
    `the claimant has consulted a lawyer about a possible claim` IS FALSE
    `the day the claimant first consulted a lawyer about it`     IS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000
#ASSERT `the days in the MAI s 37(2) period for` `Grace's notice facts` EQUALS 88
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`MAI s 37(2)-(3) -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 88 TRUE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim` 88)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Late, identified car: after the period (noticed at day 89) the obligation continues with no end; a notice with an
-- excuse on day 400 fulfils it.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`MAI s 37(2)-(3) -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 88 TRUE 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim` 89), (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim, with a reasonable excuse for the delay` 400)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Unidentified car: 5 August 2025 is day 26 + 30 + 31 + 5 = 92; 5 February 2026 is day 92 + 26 (to 31 August) + 30 +
-- 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 5 = 276; the second window, from day 93, is 276 - 92 - 1 = 183 days, ending on day 276.
#ASSERT `the days in the MAI s 37(2) period for` `the unidentified car's notice facts` EQUALS 92
#ASSERT `the days after the MAI s 37(2) period to the bar for` `the unidentified car's notice facts` EQUALS 183
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`MAI s 37(2)-(3) -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 92 FALSE 183) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim` 93), (EVENT `the claimant` `give notice of the claim, with a reasonable excuse for the delay` 276)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "MAI s 37(3): notice was not given to the Nominal Defendant within 9 months ..." (notice on day 277)
#TRACE `MAI s 37(2)-(3) -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` 92 FALSE 183 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 93)
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `give notice of the claim, with a reasonable excuse for the delay` AT 277

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 7. Age and special assistance; lapse. HYPOTHETICAL: Harold, born 1 March 1960, is pushed over in a street
-- on 2 March 2025 (an assault, category D) and bruised. He then does not answer the assessor for months.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- Category D. Category C circumstances (b): not a series, and he was over 60. Category B needs a serious injury, a
-- series or a deprivation of liberty too: a bodily injury alone is one kind. So category C, $6,000.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1960) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category C` 6000)
-- With a mental illness as well (a serious injury, 2 kinds) and over 60: category B circumstances, $9,000.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1960) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category B` 9000)
-- With a very serious bodily injury (loss of function, permanent): category A circumstances, $15,000.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1960) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category A` 15000)
-- READING (finding 7): "over 60 years". Born 2 March 1965, he turns 60 on the day of the act: not over 60, so $3,000.
-- Born 1 March 1965, he turned 60 the day before: over 60, $6,000.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 1965) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category D` 3000)
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1965) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category C` 6000)
-- "a child under 16": born 2 March 2009, 16 on the day: not under 16, $3,000. Born 3 March 2009: under 16, $6,000.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2009) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category D` 3000)
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 3 3 2009) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category C` 6000)
-- A series of related crimes against a 40-year-old: category C circumstances (a), $6,000 for a category D act.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1985) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category C` 6000)
-- Over 60 at the last crime of a series (born 1 May 1965; series 2 March to 2 June 2025): category B circumstances,
-- $9,000 (a series, and over 60 when one of the acts was committed).
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 5 1965) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 6 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`special assistance` `category D` `category B` 9000)
-- A parent secondary victim gets no special assistance: s 42 has no such component.
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `parent secondary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 1960) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `no special assistance: only a primary victim gets it (s 39(h))`
-- s 61: a lapse notice on 10 June 2026; 6 months after is 10 December 2026. Contact on 9 December: did not lapse.
-- On 1 November with no contact: open if he makes contact by 10 December. On 11 December with none: lapsed.
#ASSERT `Will my application lapse` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2026) TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 9 12 2026) EQUALS `my application did not lapse: I made contact in time (s 61(4))`
#ASSERT `Will my application lapse` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 11 2026) EQUALS (`my application stays open if I make contact by` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 12 2026))
#ASSERT `Will my application lapse` TRUE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 11 12 2026) EQUALS `my application has lapsed (s 61(4)); I may apply again within the time limit (s 61(5))`
#ASSERT `Will my application lapse` FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2026) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 11 12 2026) EQUALS `my application cannot lapse unless I am given a notice under s 61, which may be given after 6 months without contact`
-- The s 61 rule. Day 0 is 10 June 2026; 10 December 2026 is day 20 + 31 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 10 = 183.
#ASSERT `the number of days from` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 6 2026) `to` (DATE_FROM_DMY 10 12 2026) EQUALS 183
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 61 -- after a lapse notice, the applicant must contact the government assessor within 6 months` 183) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `contact the government assessor` 183)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant, "s 61(4): the applicant did not contact the government assessor within 6 months ..." (day 184)
#TRACE `s 61 -- after a lapse notice, the applicant must contact the government assessor within 6 months` 183 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `contact the government assessor` AT 184

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 8. Outside the encoding, and not a victim. HYPOTHETICAL acts.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- An act of violence on 1 September 2024, the day before the version deposited: the money and time questions answer
-- `not covered`. On 2 September 2024 it is covered: Mia's figures, 27,350.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) FALSE FALSE 3000 4500 300 800 12000 250 2000 0 0 0 700 FALSE 0 0 `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2024) FALSE FALSE 3000 4500 300 800 12000 250 2000 0 0 0 700 FALSE 0 0 `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 12 6 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 15 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 27350)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for victim assistance` `primary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) EQUALS `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
#ASSERT `By when must I apply for funeral expense assistance` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 2000) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 10 2024) EQUALS `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
#ASSERT `How much funeral expense assistance can I get` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) TRUE FALSE 10000 0 EQUALS `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
#ASSERT `What special assistance can I get` `primary victim` `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 9 2024) FALSE EQUALS `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024 (transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply)`
-- s 25(1)(a): committed outside Queensland: not an act of violence.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no victim assistance: what happened is not an act of violence (ss 25, 25A)`
-- s 25A(2)(b): a lawful arrest by a police officer acting under an Act is not a crime; not domestic violence either.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no victim assistance: what happened is not an act of violence (ss 25, 25A)`
-- s 25(2): domestic violence that is not an offence is still an act of violence: a primary victim.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` (LIST `primary victim`))
-- s 26(6): the person who committed the act is not a victim of it, even if injured.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no victim assistance: a person who committed the act is not a victim of it (s 26(6))`
-- Finding 1: someone harmed intervening to help, but not injured by the act being committed against them or by
-- witnessing it, is a victim under s 5(1)(c) but not a primary, secondary or related victim (s 26).
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no victim assistance: a victim within s 5, but not a primary, secondary or related victim of the act (s 26)`
-- A parent of an injured child who is upset but not injured: a victim under s 5(1)(b), not a parent secondary victim.
-- Injured on becoming aware: a parent secondary victim (s 26(3)).
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no victim assistance: a victim within s 5, but not a primary, secondary or related victim of the act (s 26)`
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS (`eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` (LIST `parent secondary victim`))
-- No harm at all: not a victim.
#ASSERT `Am I a victim who can get assistance, and in which capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no victim assistance: not a victim of the act (ss 5, 26)`
-- A parent secondary victim's figures (s 41, 42): counselling 3,000 + medical 1,000; loss of earnings 8,000 only with
-- exceptional circumstances. Without: 4,000 + legal 500 = 4,500. With: 12,000 + 500 = 12,500.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `parent secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE 3000 1000 0 0 8000 0 0 0 0 0 500 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 4500)
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `parent secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE TRUE 3000 1000 0 0 8000 0 0 0 0 0 500 FALSE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 12500)
-- Finding 8: a parent secondary victim paid workers' compensation is outside s 31, so s 32 does not cut the figures.
#ASSERT `What is the most victim assistance I can be granted` `parent secondary victim` (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE FALSE 3000 1000 0 0 8000 0 0 0 0 0 500 TRUE 0 0 `assault` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 1 1990) (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS (`the most I can be granted, in Australian dollars, is` 4500)

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 9. Restrictions on a grant (ss 21, 78-82). HYPOTHETICAL variations on a primary victim's facts.
-- =====================================================================================================================
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no grant: not eligible for the assistance (s 78)`
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no grant: committed or conspired to commit the act (ss 21(2)(a), 26(6), 79)`
-- s 80(1): the primary victim's criminal activity was the main reason: no grant, whatever they knew.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no grant: the primary victim's criminal activity was the only or main reason for the act (ss 21(2)(b), 80(1))`
-- s 82(1)(a)(i): no reasonable help with the police investigation, no excuse: no grant. (2): with an excuse: none.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no grant: reasonable assistance was not given to the police investigation, or to an arrest or prosecution it prevented, without a reasonable excuse (ss 21(3)(b), 82)`
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`
-- Finding 5: not helping the prosecution bars a grant under s 82(1)(b) only if it prevented the arrest or prosecution.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no grant: reasonable assistance was not given to the police investigation, or to an arrest or prosecution it prevented, without a reasonable excuse (ss 21(3)(b), 82)`
-- s 82(1)(a)(ii) is only for a crime: domestic violence that is not a crime, with no help to a prosecution, is not barred.
#ASSERT `Is anything stopping a grant to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`

-- =====================================================================================================================
-- CASE 10. Paying back (ss 100, 106G, 123, 126), and the other small questions.
-- =====================================================================================================================
-- s 100(1)(b): $5,000 interim paid, $3,000 granted: refund 2,000. s 100(2): application refused: refund 5,000.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `interim assistance was more than my grant, or my application was refused (s 100)` 5000 3000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `interim assistance was more than my grant, or my application was refused (s 100)` 5000 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 5000
-- s 100(1)(a): $5,000 interim against a $27,350 grant: nothing to refund; 22,350 still to pay (checked below).
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `interim assistance was more than my grant, or my application was refused (s 100)` 5000 27350 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the assistance still to be paid after interim assistance` 27350 5000 EQUALS 22350
-- s 106G: $20,000 paid, the grant amended to $14,000 for an uncounted relevant payment: refund 6,000.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `my grant was amended for an uncounted relevant payment (s 106G)` 20000 14000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 6000
-- s 123: convicted of a fraud offence about the application, the prosecution proving the grant rested on it: all
-- $10,000 paid. Without that proof, s 123 does not apply: 0.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `I was convicted of a fraud offence about my application (s 123)` 10000 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `I was convicted of a fraud offence about my application (s 123)` 10000 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- s 126: $8,000 paid, the grant reduced on review to $8,500 (still above what was paid): nothing. To $6,500: 1,500.
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `my grant was reduced on review (s 126)` 8000 8500 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much must I pay back` `my grant was reduced on review (s 126)` 8000 6500 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1500
-- The refund rule: day 0 is the day the refund falls due. A refund of 2,000 on day 30 fulfils it; nothing to refund is
-- fulfilled at once.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 100, 106G, 123, 126 -- the person must refund the amount to the State` 2000) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` (`refund to the State` 2000) 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 100, 106G, 123, 126 -- the person must refund the amount to the State` 0) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant` `apply for internal review` 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Finding 13: no time is set for a refund. Paying 1,500 instead of 2,000 does not count, and 2,000 years on the debt is
-- still owed but never breached by time.
-- expect: the rule still waiting: PARTY the applicant MUST refund to the State 2000 (no breach)
#TRACE `ss 100, 106G, 123, 126 -- the person must refund the amount to the State` 2000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant` DOES `refund to the State` 1500 AT 30
    (WAITUNTIL 730000)
-- s 24: death of the applicant at each stage.
#ASSERT `What happens if I die` `entitled, but had not applied` EQUALS `the entitlement does not pass to the estate (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I die` `had applied, but the application was not decided` EQUALS `the application lapses (s 24(2)); the entitlement does not pass to the estate (s 24(1))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I die` `had been granted assistance, not yet paid` EQUALS `the assistance is taken never to have been granted, and the application lapses (s 24(3))`
#ASSERT `What happens if I die` `had been paid the assistance` EQUALS `s 24 says nothing about assistance already paid`
-- s 51(4): an adult with an impaired capacity who has no guardian but an administrator: the administrator. With a
-- guardian: the guardian. With none of them: a member of the support network, or someone approved. s 51(5): an adult
-- who needs help: the victim, or someone approved.
#ASSERT `Who may make my application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the victim's administrator`)
#ASSERT `Who may make my application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the victim's guardian`)
#ASSERT `Who may make my application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `a member of the victim's support network`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`)
#ASSERT `Who may make my application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS (LIST `the victim`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`)
#ASSERT `Who may make my application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS (LIST `the victim`)
-- s 52: all three: meets it; without the consent: does not.
#ASSERT `Does my application meet the form requirements` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Does my application meet the form requirements` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- ss 59, 60: before the decision, withdraw or amend (including the capacity); after it, not.
#ASSERT `Can I still withdraw or change my application` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I still withdraw or change my application` TRUE)
-- The date helpers: 29 February 2024 + 3 years is 28 February 2027 (READING); 31 May 2025 + 9 months is 28 February
-- 2026.
#ASSERT `the day that is` 3 `years after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 29 2 2024) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the day that is` 9 `months after` (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 5 2025) EQUALS DATE_FROM_DMY 28 2 2026
